2 CONT Bapt. Fjelberg pr.gj. 1869 No. Ø 2: https://media.digitalarkivet.no/view/7004/25
2 CONT
2 CONT To America.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/115486142/john-e-nerem
2 CONT
2 CONT John Nerem was the son of Ingemor Nerem and Cecelia Thorsdatter
2 CONT
2 CONT John married Alice Thompson on April 16, 1896. The six children to this union were:
2 CONT 1) Edward Severin Nerem (5 Feb 1897-Nov 1980)[FAG#168229019]
2 CONT 2) Rancy "Ruth" Amanda Nerem (Mrs. William J. Amundson)(29 Jul 1898-May 1985)[FAG#34669297]
2 CONT 3) Alfred John Nerem (8 May 1901-5 Feb 1962)
2 CONT 4) Infant Nerem
2 CONT 5) Infant Nerem
2 CONT 6) Infant Nerem
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT Obituary transcribed by Dena Gray-Fisher, source: Roland Record, March 30, 1961
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary of John Nerem
2 CONT John Nerem was born at Bergen Norway, December 23, 1869, and passed away March 15, 1961, at the Mary Greeley hospital in Ames, Iowa, at the age of 91 years, two months and 20 days. He immigrated to the United states in 1889, comin
2 CONC g to Slater, Iowa. He then moved to Roland where he was employed for a number of years.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 16, 1896, he was united in marriage to Alice Thompson at Roland. To this union six children were born. Three children died in infancy, while Ed, Alfred and Ruth Amundson survive. He and his family farmed in the Roland and
2 CONC  Radcliffe community until he retired and moved to Roland where he resided until five weeks ago when he entered the Mary Greeley Hospital in Ames, where he was a patient until the time of his death.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Nerem was preceded in death by his wife, Alice, three children, four brothers, and one sister. He is survived by his children, Ed of Roland, Alfred of Slater, and Ruth Amundson of Ames. Also surviving are 14 grandchildren, 2 g
2 CONC reat grandchildren, two great, great grandchildren, and a host of relatives and friends.
