1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/50076412/lars-amdall
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Amdall BIRTH	4 Nov 1853 Sauda kommune, Rogaland fylke, Norway DEATH	2 May 1941 (aged 87) Story City, Story County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Roland Cemetery Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary source, The Roland Record, May 8, 1941 "THREE FUNERALS HELD PAST WEEK SERVICES CONDUCTED FROM BERGEN LUTHERAN CHURCH
2 CONT
2 CONT Three deaths occurred the past week of residents of this community, and funeral services were held Saturday, Monday and Wednesday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oscar M. Wierson died Thursday last week and his funeral was held Saturday; Lars Amdall passed away at the Old People's Home in Story City Friday and was buried on Monday, and Mrs. Helen Johnson died in Chicago Monday and services
2 CONC  were conducted on Wednesday. Burials were all made in the Roland cemetery. [Submitter has omitted the obituary sections pertaining to Oscar M. Wierson and Helen Johnson, which are on separate records.]
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars G. Amdall, who suffered a stroke on April 28, died at the Story City hospital on Friday morning.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were conducted on Monday afternoon with a short service at the Old Peoples Home in Story City, where he had made his home for the past two years, and at Bergen Lutheran church in Roland at 2 o'clock. Rev. M.O. Sum
2 CONC stad was in charge, and Rev. Peder Buland, superintendent of the Old Peoples Home, assisted. Burial was made in the Roland cemetery. The pall bearers wer Carroll and Leslie Pearson, Arnold Skartvedt, Marvin Sandwick, Clifford Amda
2 CONC ll and Arlo Stukenberg.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those from a distance in attendance at the funeral were Mr. and Mrs. C. T. Thorresen, Mrs. Raymond Hereim, and Gilbert Amdall of Wallingford, Mrs. Earl Fenn of Colfax and Mrs. Walter Fox of Newton.
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars G. Amdall was born in Sauda, Norway on November 4, 1853, son of Gunder and Martha Amdall (Aasen), and died at the Story City hospital on May 2, 1941, at the age of 87 years, 6 months and 28 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to this country in 1874. On Februrary 4, 1887, he was united in marriage to Jane Twedt, who survives him. To this union seven children were born: Gehard Amdall of McCallsburg; Mrs. Sam Arnold (Julia) of Seattle, Wash.; Mrs
2 CONC . Christ Holt (Martha), and Mrs. John Thorsness (Lena), of Story City; Mrs. Clarence Pearson (Clara) of Radcliffe; Mrs. Stanton Israel (Hannah) of Prairie View, Ill., and Mrs. Arne Sandvik (Mabel) of McCallsburg, all of who, toget
2 CONC her with their mother, survive him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also survived by 29 grandchildren, and 11 great grandchildren; also one brother, Knudt G. Amdall of Kerkhove, Minn., and a sister, Mrs. Ragnela Peterson of Estherville.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Amdall lived for many years on a farm three miles southeast of Roland. In 1902 he moved with his family to Dallas, Wis., where they farmed for nine years, returning to this vicinity in 1911. On March 6, 1939, Mr. and Mrs. Amda
2 CONC ll entered the Old Peoples Home at Story City where they have since resided."
2 CONT
2 CONT Plot: C-18, 532, 1 Latitude: 42.164800 Longitude: -93.516678 Name: Lars G. Amdall Birth Date: Nov. 4, 1853 in Sauda, Norway Death Date: May 2, 1941 in Story City, Story County, Iowa
