2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/175605431/thor-e-nerem
2 CONT
2 CONT Thor E. Nerem was the son of E. Nerem and Susana.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Susan Peterson on December 28, 1886, at the Plattville Church, Minooka, Grundy county, Illinois. To this union four children were born.
2 CONT 1) Edward "Eddie" T. Nerem (21 Oct 1887-25 Apr 1955)[FAQ#122894195]
2 CONT 2) Sam Oliy Nerem (30 Oct 1889-21 Sep 1980)[FAQ#122897080]
2 CONT 3) Ole Selmer Nerem (20 Apr 1892-24 Jan 1942){FAQ#1228945145]
2 CONT 4) Sadie Emelia Nerem (Mrs. Bakken)(29 Mar 1896-
2 CONT
2 CONT His wife preceded him in death April 12, 1902.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married again on April 20, 1909, to Mrs. Marie Ljusness. There were no children to this union.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT Obituary transcribed by Dena Gray-Fisher, source: Roland Record, July 27, 1932
2 CONT
2 CONT OBITUARY
2 CONT
2 CONT Thor Nerem was born in Olen, Norway, on October 4, 18858, and died July 15, 1932, at Forest City, at the age of 73 years, 9 months and 11 days. The cause of his death was cancer of the stomach and he had been ill about four months
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT He came to this country in 1880 and settled in Grundy county, Ill., and a few later came to Roland where he lived until 1910, when the family moved to Forest City.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married in 1886 to Miss Susan Peterson and to this union four children were born. They are Ed T., Sam O., and Ole S. Nerem, and Mrs. Sadie Bakken, all of whom survive him. His wife preceded him in death April 12, 1902. He w
2 CONC as married again on April 20, 1909, to Mrs. Marie Ljusness, who survives him.
2 CONT
2 CONT Besides his wife and the four children, he leaves two stepdaughters, Mrs. Agnes Quintus of Garner and Mrs. Walter Horwedell of Sterling, Ill., three brothers, Martin and John Nerem of Roland and Torres Nerem of Story City, and nin
2 CONC e grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held at Immanuel Lutheran church in Forest City, of which he was a member, on Monday forenoon, July 18, Rev. N. O. Peterson of Morris, Minn., a brother-in-law of the deceased, officiating assisted by Prof. Os
2 CONC car Hanson. Prof. Odvin Hagen sang two solos. The remains were then taken to Roland where a service was held in the afternoon at Salem Lutheran church, Rev. Olaf Holen officiating, assisted by Rev. Peterson. O. S. Boyd sang two so
2 CONC los at this service. Interment was made in the Roland cemetery.
