1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Roland Record, June 23, 1949
2 CONT NONOGENARIAN PASSED AWAY
2 CONT SERVICES WERE HELD TUESDAY AT SUNSET HOME AND IN BERGEN CHURCH
2 CONT Funeral services were held for Ole B. Anderson from the Sunset Home Chapel at Story City at one o'clock Tuesday afternoon, June 21, with Rev. E.R. Rorem conducting the services in the absence of his regular pastor, Rev. Allen E. N
2 CONC elson.
2 CONT
2 CONT A vocal solo was given by Mrs. Peterson, the home nurse who had helped care for Mr. Anderson. She sang "The Land Where They Never Grow Old," accompanied by Mr. Otto J. Hanson. A vocal solo was rendered by Otto J. Hanson, "Sleep Th
2 CONC e Last Sleep," also accompanied by Mrs. Hanson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Services at the Bergen church were held at two o'clock with Rev. Rorem in charge. Special music consisted of a song by the audience, "What a Friend We Have in Jesus", a vocal solo by Mrs. Grant Eggland, "I Know of a Sleep in Jesus
2 CONC ' Name". After the sermon Otto J. Hanson sang "Den Store Vide Flok" accompanied by Mrs. Hanson at the organ.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall bearers were six nephews of Mr. Anderson: Floyd Anderson, Oscar Anderson, Howard Anderson, Casper Thompson, Herman Ryan, and Clarence Ryg. He was laid to rest in the Roland cemetery by the side of his wife. Blessed be his mem
2 CONC ory.
2 CONT
2 CONT A great number of relatives and friends were present at the services. They were from Kelley, Huxley, Slater, New Sharon, Des Moines, Nevada, Forest City, Clarion, Manly, McCallsburg, Story City, Ames, Badger, Garden City, Radcliff
2 CONC e, Randall, Zearing, Madrid, and from Kenyon, Minneapolis, and Ellendale, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ole B. Anderson was born February 5, 1858, at Saude, Norway. His parents were Ove and Barbro Birkland Anderson. At the age of 12 years he came to Story county, Iowa, with his parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was confirmed in 1872 in the St. Petri church one mile east of Story City, and grew to manhood in this community.
2 CONT
2 CONT On May 7, 1888, he was married to Anna Ryan in Livingston County, Ill. They came to Iowa and started housekeeping on a farm four and a half miles southeast of Roland, where they lived 36 years. In April, 1924, they moved to Roland
2 CONC  where they resided until the death of Mrs. Anderson on October 19, 1930.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Anderson made his home with his children until February, 1948, when he entered the Sunset Home at Story City, where he passed away June 18, 1949, at the age of 91 years, 4 months and 13 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT He leaves to mourn his passing, one daughter, Mrs. Agnes Minde of Roland; two sons, Nels of Clarion, and Otis B. Anderson of Roland. Also surviving are five grandchildren, Mrs. Maxine Bicknell of Los Angeles, Cal., Mrs. Ardis John
2 CONC son of Boone, Marion Minde of Roland, Orvis Anderson of Des Moines, David and Jane Ann Anderson of Roland; one great grandchild, Keith Hennick of Boone; two brothers, John O. Anderson of Story City, and Johannes Anderson of New Sh
2 CONC aron; and three sisters, Nellie and Ellen Anderson, and Mrs. Martha Egenes, all of Minneapolis, Minn.
