1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Ove O. Anderson 
2 CONT Photo added by Dena Gray-Fisher
2 CONT
2 CONT Ove O. Anderson
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT 15 Apr 1866
2 CONT Norway
2 CONT Death
2 CONT 15 Feb 1936 (aged 69)
2 CONT Roland, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT Burial
2 CONT Roland Cemetery
2 CONT Howard Township, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT Show MapGPS-Latitude: 42.1649323, Longitude: -93.5164337
2 CONT Plot
2 CONT B-13, 336, 6
2 CONT Memorial ID
2 CONT 114611037 · View Source
2 CONT Memorial
2 CONT Photos 1
2 CONT Flowers 0
2 CONT
2 CONT Ove O. Anderson was the son of Ove Anderson and Aagata "Aggie" Orton
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Bertha Raymond on March 6, 1890. Bertha died June 6, 1897. To this union was born:
2 CONT 1) Oscar Olia Anderson (15 May 1891-1958)[Find A Grave Memorial# 132134311]
2 CONT 2) Lars Severin Anderson (9 Feb 1893-18 Sep 1962)[Find A Grave Memorial# 52693721]
2 CONT 3) Amanda Josephine Anderson (Mrs. George Reng)(23 Feb 1895-9 Jul 1976)[Find A Grave Memorial# 169716038]
2 CONT 4) Betty Anderson (3 Jun 1897-1897),died in infancy
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Oliva Amalia Osmundson on July 2, 1898. Oliva died in 1901. The children to this union were:
2 CONT 1) Julia Anderson (Mrs. Archie Buth) (13 Mar 1899-Dec 1975)
2 CONT 2) Ada Otelia Anderson (Mrs. Lloyd Bock)(5 Aug 1900-28 28 Dec 1998)[Find A Grave Memorial# 149034086]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Anna Ristesund on Nov. 12, 1904. To this union was born was born 11 children, six sons and five daughters.
2 CONT 1) Sherman M. Anderson (15 Sep 1905-1 Jan 1991)
2 CONT 2) Edna J. Anderson (Mrs. Ellis Heineman)(3 Feb 1907-4 Oct 1984)
2 CONT 3) Obed Archie Anderson (29 May 1909-10 Jun 1956)
2 CONT 4) Floyd R. Anderson (7 Feb 1911-16 Mar 1997)
2 CONT 5) Ruth Charlotte Anderson (Mrs. Theodore Haas) (22 Apr 1913-1977)
2 CONT 6) Myrtie Adeline Anderson (Mrs. Loren Rosheim)(8 Jun 1914-24 Sep 1995)
2 CONT 7) Lawrence H. Anderson (14 Nov 1916-27 Aug 2002)
2 CONT 8) Ethel M. Anderson (17 Aug 1919-23 Aug 2015)
2 CONT 9) Joel Selmer Anderson (18 Sep 1921-5 Mar 2006)
2 CONT 10) Ralph A. Anderson (28 Apr 1924-31 Mar 2013)
2 CONT 11) Jacquelin Patricia Anderson (Mrs. Howard Corpening)(26 Oct 1927-13 May 2015)
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------------------------
2 CONT Obituary transcribed by Dena Gray-Fisher, source: Roland Record, February 26, 1936
2 CONT
2 CONT Ove O. Anderson was born at Saude, Norway, April 15, 1866, and died at his home west of Roland February 15, 1936, at the age of 69 years and 10 months.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was the son of Ove and Aagatha Anderson and came to America with his parents in 1870. The family lived for a short time 3 miles southwest of Roland, later moving to the Anderson homestead 5 miles south of town.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Anderson was married three times and was the father of seventeen children, sixteen of whom survive him.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married to Bertha Raymond in February 1890, and they made their home at Sioux Rapids. Four children were born to this union, one of whom died in infancy. Those surviving are Oscar Anderson and Mrs. George Reng of Sioux Rapi
2 CONC ds, and Lars Anderson of Chester. Mrs. Anderson died June 6, 1897.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married again to Oleva Osmundson in July 1898, and two children were born to them. Julia Anderson of Des Moines, and Mrs. Lloyd Bock of Minneapolis, Minn. His wife died in 1901.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was married again on November 12, 1904, to Anna Ristesund, who survives him. Eleven children were born to them, all of whom survive. They are, Mrs. Leonard Lyles of Clinton, Mrs. Howard Corpening of Saratoga, Wyo., Sherman, Obe
2 CONC d, Floyd, Myrtie, Lawrence, Ethyl, Joel, Ralph and Patricia, at home.
2 CONT
2 CONT He also leaves four brothers. O. B. Anderson of Clarion, J. O. Anderson of Story City, J. T. Anderson of Nevada, and M. O. Anderson of Roland, and three sisters, Ellen and Nellie Anderson of Minneapolis, Minn., and Mrs. John Egene
2 CONC s of Renwick, and four grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT After residing at Sioux Rapids for a number of years, Mr. Anderson came to Roland. He took a trip to Norway and visited with relatives for a while and on his return purchased the farm just west of town where he now resided. He has
2 CONC  lived there since that time with the exception of two years, in 1908 and 1909, when he lived in Colorado.
2 CONT
2 CONT He had been failing in health for several years and had been confined to his home during the winter.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was held at the home and at Bergen church, of which he was an active member, on Tuesday afternoon, Rev. M. O. Sumstad officiating. Interment was made in the Roland cemetery. Owing to the blocked roads, only a few of hi
2 CONC s relatives and friends were able to get her for the funeral. His children in northern Iowa were snowbound and could not get here.
2 CONT
2 CONT The pall bearers were M. O. Anderson, O. M. Rierson, H. H. Severeid, O. M. Thompson, A. E. Humphrey and Howard Anderson. Music was furnished by a mixed group.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those present from a distance were Mrs. Lloyd Bock, Ellen and Nellie Anderson, of Minneapolis, Minn., Mrs. Howard Corpening of Saratoga, Wyo., Mrs. Sam Klingen of Laramie, Wyo., Mrs. Leonard C. Lyles of Clinton, and Julia Anderson
2 CONC  of Des Moines, Mr. and Mrs. Richard Anderson and J. T. Anderson of Nevada, and J. O. Anderson and Mrs. I. G. Grindem of Story City, arrived here later in the afternoon after the road from Story City had been cleared.
