1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT In October 1939, Martin Anderson underwent a surgery and was recovering when he suffered a heart attack in November which took his life.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was born to Ove and Aagote(Orton) Anderson on Nov. 3, 1872. On April 27, 1899, he married Mary Hegland. From this union were born six children, Orvel, Amos, Orphie, Belford, Milvern and Florence.
2 CONT
2 CONT After their marriage, the couple started farming south of Roland where they lived until 1910 when they moved to Roland and Mr. Anderson entered the garage business with his brother J.T. Anderson. In 1918 he purchased the farm a mi
2 CONC le west of Roland where the family lived until moving back to town.
2 CONT
2 CONT He leaves his wife, three children, four grandchildren, his aged father-in-law, M. Hegland who has made his home with them in recent years, and three sistes, Mrs. John Egenes of Roland and Misses Ellen and Nellie Anderson of Minne
2 CONC apolis, and three brothers, Ole B. Anderson of Roland, J.O. Anderson of Story City, and J.T. Anderson of Des Moines.
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral was held Tuesday afternoon at the home and at Bergen church with Rev. M.O. Sumstad officiating assisted by Rev. O. Amdalsrud. Interment was made in the Roland cemetery. Special music consisted of a duet by Mr. and Mr.s
2 CONC . O.S. Boyd at the residence and a solo by Mrs. O.E. Ritland and another duet by Mr. and Mrs. Boyd at the church. Pall bearers were nephews of the deceased, Harold O. Hegland, Lester, Irvin, Sherman, Howard and Otis B. Anderson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those from a distance attending the funeral included Mrs. T.S. Erickson and M.C. Erickson of Sioux Falls, S.D., and Mr. and Mrs. Lawrence.
