2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary transcribed by Dena Gray-Fisher, source: Roland Record, October 22, 1953
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary of J. T. Anderson
2 CONT
2 CONT Johannes T. Anderson was born May 13, 1876 in Milford township, on the Anderson farm four and one-half miles south of Roland. He was a son of Ove and Aagata Anderson and one of twelve children, seven brothers and five sisters. He 
2 CONC was baptized in the St. Petri Lutheran church, which was located one mile east of Story City at that time. He was confirmed in Bergen Lutheran church, by Rev. C. B. Jacobson.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the fall of 1899 Mr. Anderson bought the Anderson homestead of 320 acres, which he farmed until he moved to Roland in 1909.
2 CONT
2 CONT March 20, 1901, he was married to Bessie Malenda Egeland in the Bergen Lutheran church. To this union were born eight children, all of whom survive him. The are Alma (Mrs. Irwin Grindem) of Nevada; Bernice (Mrs. O. C. Meyer) of De
2 CONC s Moines; Dr. Lester Anderson of Kingsville, Texas, Juen (Mrs. L. A. Chambers) of Fort Dodge; Mildred (Mrs. J. M. Newman) of Seattle, Wash.; Willard Anderson in the U.S. Navy; Marvin and Allan Anderson of Seattle, Wash.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1909 the family moved to Roland where Mr. Anderson went into the automobile business which he conducted until 1917. While farming in Milford township he was director of the Milford township school for eight years, and also serv
2 CONC ed as director of the Roland school board after moving to Roland, for two terms. He also served as assessor in Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1919 the family moved to the farm one mile south and a half mile west of Roland where they lived until 1928, when they moved back to Roland. In 1931 they moved to Nevada where Mr. Anderson was with the Farmers Oil Corporation u
2 CONC ntil 1936 when they moved to Des Moines.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Anderson died on New Years Day in 1941. In 1942 Mr. Anderson moved to New Sharon where he resided at the home of a distant relative, Ollie Johnson, until his death on September 29, 1953, at the home of his daughter Mrs. C. O.
2 CONC  Meyer in Des Moines, at the age of 77 years, four months and 16 days. Besides his eight children he is survived by two sisters, Ellen and Nellie Anderson of Minneapolis, Minn.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services were held on Saturday, October 3, at the Erickson Funeral Home and at Bergen Lutheran church in Roland, with Rev. Frederick J. Weertz, pastor of St. John's Lutheran church in Des Moines, in charge, assisted by Rev
2 CONC . Allen E. Nelson. Burial was mad in the Roland cemetery.
