2 CONT Source: 1. Oregon Death Index certificate #3528 2. World War I Draft Registration Card (gives birth year a 1889) 3. North Dakota Military Men 1917-1918 Roster of the Men and Women Who Served in the Army or Naval Service (Including
2 CONC  the Marine Corps) of the United States or its Allies from the State of North Dakota in the World War, 1917-1918 Volume 4 Rich to Zygmond
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Edward Teig  Army #: 2,354,239 Registrant: yes, Dunn county Birth Place: Story county, Iowa Birth Date: 18 Aug 1888 Parent's Origin: of Norwegian parents Occupation: farmer Comment: enlisted at Bismarck, on Oct. 8, 1917; sen
2 CONC t to Jefferson Barracks, Mo.; served in Medical Officers Training Camp, Fort Riley, Kans., to Nov. 15, 1917; Ambulance Company No. 16, Medical Department, to discharge. Grade: Wagoner, Dec. 4, 1917; overseas from April 10, 1918, t
2 CONC o Aug. 4, 1919. Engagements: Defensive: Aisne. Offensives: Aisne-Marne; St. Mihiel; Meuse-Argonne. Defensive Sectors: Chateau-Thierry (Ile-de-France); Limey and Marbache (Lorraine). Discharged at Camp Dodge, Iowa, on Aug. 14, 1919
2 CONC , as a Wagoner. 
