1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/119591276/anna-mary-teig
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Mary Grove Teig
2 CONT BIRTH	13 Oct 1876
2 CONT Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT DEATH	24 Oct 1961 (aged 85)
2 CONT Story City, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Roland Cemetery
2 CONT Howard Township, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary source, The Roland Record, November 11, 1961
2 CONT
2 CONT "Last rites held for Mrs. Mary Teig
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Mary Teig were held Wednesday afternoon, November 1, at Bergen Lutheran Church, with the Rev. Howard M. Lybeck officiating. Oris J. Osheim sang "Rock of Ages" and Otto J. Hanson sang "Den Store Hvide Flok
2 CONC ".
2 CONT
2 CONT The pall bearers were grandsons of Mrs. Teig: Duane Osheim of Decorah, Paul Teig of Iowa Falls, Keith McKinney of Colo, Loren Teig of Ellsworth, Richard Teig and Dwight Osheim of Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial was in the Roland cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Teig passed away Sunday noon, October 29, 1961, at Story City Memorial Hospital at the age of 85 years and 16 days. She was the daughter of Mr. and Mrs. Mons C. Grove, who were among the first pioneers to settle in the R
2 CONC oland area of Story County. She was born October 13, 1876, at the family homestead three-quarters of a mile south of Roland. She was baptized Anna Marie Grove on November 2, 1876, by Rev. Ingvald Eistenson of Salem Church. She was
2 CONC  confirmed October 18, 1891, by Rev. C. C. Holter.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 31, 1903, she was married to Knut P. Teig by Rev. J.N. Sandven. She and her husband lived on her parents' farm for one year, then they moved to their own farm two miles east and one mile south of Roland, where they res
2 CONC ided for 44 years. After retirement they lived in Roland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Seven children were born to this union. Mrs. Teig is survived by four sons and two daughters. They are Palmer G. of McCallsburg, Mons A. of Ellsworth, Hubert E. of Roland, Kermit M. of West Union; Mrs. Victor (Virginia) McKinney o
2 CONC f Colo, Mrs. Orris J. (Ellen) Osheim of Roland. One son, Edward, a twin to Ellen, passed away in infancy.
2 CONT
2 CONT She also leaves 20 grandchildren and two great granddaughters. One sister, Mrs. Emma McCord of Nevada, also survives. Her husband, Knut P. Teig, passed away October 9, 1951.
2 CONT
2 CONT There were friends and relatives attending from Dover, St. Paul, Minneapolis and Northfield, all in Minnesota; West Union, Des Moines, Ames, Story City, Ellsworth, Colo, McCallsburg, Clemons, Zearing, and Nevada."
