1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/137635089/bertha-ingeborg-tunheim
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Ingeborg Moen Tunheim
2 CONT BIRTH	17 Mar 1915
2 CONT DEATH	21 Oct 2014 (aged 99)
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Oak Grove Cemetery
2 CONT Newfolden, Marshall County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Tunheim of Newfolden, MN age 99 died peacefully on Tuesday, October 21, 2014 at Thief River Care Center in Thief River Falls, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Service to Celebrate the Life of Bertha Tunheim will be held at 2:00 PM on Saturday, October 25, 2014 at the New Hope Lutheran Church in Newfolden, MN with Pastor Ollie Urdahl officiating. Burial will be at Oak Grove Cemet
2 CONC ery in Newfolden, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Visitation will be held 5:00 PM until 8:00 PM with a 7:00 PM prayer service on Friday October 24, 2014 at Johnson Funeral Service in Thief River Falls, MN. Visitation will also be held for one hour prior to the funeral at New Hope
2 CONC  Lutheran Church on Saturday.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha Ingeborg Moen was born on March 17, 1915 in Spruce Valley Township, Marshall County, MN the daughter of Andrew and Alida (Iverson) Moen. She was baptized and confirmed in the Lutheran faith. She attended Monroe Country Scho
2 CONC ol in Spruce Valley Township.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha worked at various jobs in the Newfolden, MN area. On December 24, 1941, Bertha was united in marriage to Joseph Tunheim in Viking, MN. They made their home on a farm north of Newfolden in New Maine Township and to this unio
2 CONC n two children were born, Arlynn and Mona. In the fall of 1952, the family moved into Newfolden.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha worked cleaning for the Newfolden School for many years and later worked at the Land-O-Lakes Turkey Plant in Thief River Falls, MN. In 1977 she started working with the meals at the Newfolden Senior Center until retiring in
2 CONC  the late 1980’s.
2 CONT
2 CONT She enjoyed visiting with family and friends, especially enjoyed spending her holidays with the Berggren and Lee families, gardening, baking lefse and donuts, sewing, music, and listening to Trumpet of Truth radio program on Sunda
2 CONC y evenings.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha was a member of the New Hope Lutheran Church in Newfolden, MN where she enjoyed singing with the New Hope Singers and was active in the Women’s Group. She never missed church on Sunday and also enjoyed the Bible Studies. Be
2 CONC rtha was also a member of the Newfolden American Legion Auxiliary, a girl scout leader for many years, and was active in the Newfolden Senior Citizen group.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include her son, Arlynn (Donna) Tunheim of Newfolden, MN; son-in-law, Juan Castro of Sheffield Lake, OH; grandchildren, Kelly (Scott) Van Meter of Sheffield Lake, OH, Shawn Castro of Warren, PA, Nancy Tunheim of Newfolde
2 CONC n, MN and Heidi Tunheim of Thief River Falls, MN; great-grandchildren, Cristina Castro, Nicholas Van Meter and Alexander Van Meter; and many nieces, nephews, relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bertha is preceded in death by her husband, Joseph in 1975; daughter, Mona Castro in 1977; and siblings, Knute (Mary) Moen, Inga (Clarence) Kezar, John “Henry” (Zephra) Moen, Arthur (Louise) Moen, Borghild (Elman) Rehder, Magnus “
2 CONC Manny” Moen.
