1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/30484010/hannah-amanda-israel
2 CONT
2 CONT Baxter Bulletin. Mountain Home, Arkansas. 19 Apr. 1991, Fri.
2 CONT Visitation today for Hannah Israel, 90, of MH
2 CONT Hannah Israel 90, of Mountain Home died Thursday, April 18, 1991, at Baxter County Regional Hospital.
2 CONT Services are set for Saturday at 2 p.m. at the Roller Funeral Home Chapel with the Rev. Ken Lampe officiating. Visitation is today from 9 a.m. to 9 p.m. with the family receiving friends from 6 to 8 p.m. at the Roller Funeral Home
2 CONC  and burial will be at Baxter Memorial Gardens.
2 CONT Mrs. Israel was born on Feb. 24, 1901, at Dallas, Wis., and was a homemaker. She has been a Mountain Home resident since 1977 and was formerly of Rhinelander, Wis. She was a Lutheran.
2 CONT She was preceded in death by both parents, Lars and Jane Amdall, one daughter, one brother, one grandson, and her husband, Stanton Israel.
2 CONT She is survived by two sons, Leroy and Jordan Haverson both of Mountain Home; two sisters, Clara Pearson of Story City, Iowa, and Mable Sandvich of Iowa; eight grandchildren; 19 great-grandchildren; seven great-great-grandchildren
2 CONC ; and many nieces and nephews.
2 CONT Memorials may be made to the Redeemer Lutheran Church.
2 CONT Contributor: Jean Wilson (48841367) • carmijean@yahoo.com
