1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary transcribed by Dena Gray-Fisher, source: Roland Record February 15, 1951
2 CONT
2 CONT LIFETIME ROLAND RESIDENT DIED
2 CONT
2 CONT MRS. M. O. ANDERSON PASSED AWAY WEDNESDAY NIGHT FROM HEART TROUBLE
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. M. O. Anderson, a lifetime member of the Roland community, were held Sunday, February 11, 1951, with a prayer services from Erickson funeral home at 2 p.m. and Bergen Lutheran church at 2:30, with Rev. Al
2 CONC len E. Nelson officiating. Burial was in the Roland cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. G. E. DuBois and Mrs. B. A. Imsland of McCallsburg sang "Beyond the Sunset," and the Ladies Sextet of Bergen church sang "Softly and Tenderly." There were beautiful floral offerings and many In Memoriam gifts to missions and 
2 CONC other worthy causes.
2 CONT
2 CONT The casket bearers were Harold Hegland, Otis Anderson, Joel Anderson, Henry Bakka, Reuben Solyst and Ervin Anderson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Anderson was born December 14, 1880, a daughter of Michael and Caroline Hegland. She lived her entire life in the Roland community and died at the home of her daughter and son-in-law, Mr. and Mrs. Chester Pearson, McCallsburg
2 CONC , Iowa, Wednesday evening at 10:30, at the age of 70 years, one month and 24 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 27, 1899, she was united in marriage to Martin O. Anderson, who preceded her in death on November 11, 1939. To this union six children were born, three of whom died in infancy. Those who survive to mourn her death are her
2 CONC  children, Orphie (Mrs. Chester Pearson) of McCallsburg, Belford of Sparta, Wisc., and Milvern of Chicago, Ill.; six grandchildren, Janet and Mary Ellen Pearson, Philip, Paul and Donna Anderson, and Audrey Anderson. She is also su
2 CONC rvived by one sister, Clara (Mrs. L. F. Davis) of Los Angeles, Calif., and four brothers, Lewis of Sioux Falls, S.D., Henry of Roland, Martin of Venice, Califl, and Elroy of Los Angeles, Calif., and nieces and nephews.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Anderson was a faithful member of the Bergen church which she had been a member all her life.
2 CONT
2 CONT Those from a distance attending the funeral were: Mr. and Mrs. B. A. Anderson of Sparta, Wisc.; Mr. and Mrs. M. A. Anderson of Chicago, Ill.; R. L. Hegland of Sioux Falls, S. D.; Mrs. John Egenes, Ellen and Nellie Anderson, Mrs. R
2 CONC ay Spafford, of Minneapolis, Minn.; Mr. and Mrs. L. B. Erickson of Sioux City; Mr. and Mrs. Walter Carson, Elizabeth, Philip and Ruth Ellen of Leland; Herbert Jacobson of Adel; Mrs. Robert Grummer of Madison, Wisc.; Mrs. J. O. And
2 CONC erson, Mr. and Mrs. Dick Heggen, Mr. and Mrs. Virgil Smith, Miss Betts Anderson, Dr. and Mrs. Clayton Meyer, Mrs. Lloyd Bock, of Des Moines; N. B. Anderson of Clarion, Ernest Rod of Waverly, and a host of friends and relatives fro
2 CONC m Ames, Story City, Garden City, Radcliffe, Hubbard, McCallsburg, Nevada and Zearing.
