1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/195434424/dewein-albert-lappegaard
2 CONT
2 CONT DeWein Albert Lappegaard
2 CONT BIRTH	15 Dec 1919
2 CONT Pennington County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT DEATH	13 Nov 2017 (aged 97)
2 CONT Goodridge, Pennington County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT BURIAL	
2 CONT Goodridge Cemetery
2 CONT Goodridge, Pennington County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT DeWein Lappegaard, 97, of Goodridge, MN passed away on Monday, November 13, 2017 at his residence in Goodridge, MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral service to celebrate DeWein’s life will be held at 10:30 AM on Friday, November 17, 2017 at Johnson Funeral Service in Thief River Falls, MN with Rev. Kristin Ostercamp officiating. Visitation will be held one hour prior t
2 CONC o the service. Burial will be at the Goodridge Community Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT DeWein Albert Lappegaard was born on December 15, 1919 near Rosewood in Pennington County, MN the son of Albert and Hazel (Rye) Lappegaard. He attended country school and worked on the family farm.
2 CONT
2 CONT On December 23, 1940, DeWein was united in marriage to Alice Olson and to this union eight children were born, Jerome, Louann, Arlene, Ramona, Mary Ann, Darla, Dale and Daniel. The family lived on the farm near Rosewood for a time
2 CONC  before moving into Thief River Falls, MN. On November 5, 1961, DeWein was united in marriage to Mary Couglin and to this union Marcella and Duane were born. In 1983, DeWein and his companion, Sandra Larson welcomed a daughter Sam
2 CONC antha to the family.
2 CONT
2 CONT DeWein worked as a heavy duty machine operator and mechanic throughout North Dakota, Minnesota and Wisconsin. Along with many road construction projects, DeWein helped build the crooked road from Thief River Falls to Plummer.
2 CONT
2 CONT He enjoyed hunting, fishing, dancing, pull tabs, camping and spending time with his family.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a member of the 49ers Union.
2 CONT
2 CONT Survivors include seven children, Louann (Charles), Arlene, Ramona (David), Darla (Larry), Marcella (Wayne), Duane Joseph, Samantha (Wayne); daughters-in-law, Christy & Jody; 31 grandchildren; 9 step great-grandchildren; 75 great-
2 CONC grandchildren; 8 great-great grandchildren; sister-in-law, Mayme; and a very special person, Sandra; and many other relatives and friends.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is preceded in death by his parents; wives, Alice & Mary; children, Jerome, Mary Ann (Greg) Weyer, Dale, Danny; son-in-law, Duane Bjerke; step-children, Patricia (Wally) Heaton and Kathy Rekow; grandchildren, Rodney Heaton, Ric
2 CONC k Heaton, Peggy Bjerke; 2 great-grandchildren; sisters, Ila (Archie) Lull, Marcella (Leonard) Bottom; and brother, Virgil “Sonny” Lappegaard.
2 CONT
2 CONT source: johnsonfuneralservice.com
