1 NOTE {geni:about_me} In Loving Memory of Ada A. Jackson
2 CONT December 23, 1894 – June 13, 1987
2 CONT Ada A. Jackson, age 92, passed away peacefully on Saturday, June 13, 1987, at a nursing home in Mason City, Iowa. A private memorial service was planned to honor her life and legacy.
2 CONT Born in Runnells, Iowa, on December 23, 1894, Ada was the daughter of Robert and Mary Gilliland. She spent her early years in Gowrie, where she attended school and was a member of the Methodist Church. Her faith remained a guiding
2 CONC  light throughout her life.
2 CONT Ada lived in several Iowa communities including Manly, Rock Falls, Clear Lake, and Mason City. She worked as a bookkeeper for the Salvation Army and remained active in their church after moving to Mason City.
2 CONT She was married to Leonard Jackson, who preceded her in death. Together, they raised four children:
2 CONT - Colleen Dillon (Mrs. Ken), Folsom, California
2 CONT - Arlyne Gasaway (Mrs. Donald), Mason City, Iowa
2 CONT - Dale Jackson, Redwood City, California
2 CONT - Delbert Jackson, St. Maries, Idaho
2 CONT Ada was a proud grandmother to seven grandchildren and three great-grandchildren. She was preceded in death by her husband, three brothers, and her twin sister.
2 CONT Her life was marked by quiet strength, devotion to family, and a deep sense of service. She leaves behind a legacy of kindness, resilience, and faith.
2 CONT Arrangements were handled by Hogan-Bremer Colonial Chapel, Mason City, Iowa.
