1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary - Leonard Jackson Leonard William Jackson, the son of Charles and Estella Hoyt Jackson, was born August 17, 1893 in Springview, Nebraska.  His childhood years were spent in Winterset, Iowa, and it was in that community th
2 CONC at he received his early education. Leonard was married to Ada Anna Gilleland on May 15, 1915, in Ft. Dodge, Iowa.  Throughout their marriage, they lived in a number of communities throughout Iowa and Minnesota.  Leonard worked fo
2 CONC r the Rock Island Railroad for 49 years, serving as a stationary engineer. He retired in August of 1958.  Throughout his life, Leonard enjoyed his association with people and was a very trustworthy person.  He was a member of the 
2 CONC Seventh Day Adventist Church. Mr. Jackson passed away on September 30, 1982, at the Spencer Municipal Hospital, at the age of 89 years, 1 month, and 13 days.  He was preceded in death by his parents; 2 still-born children; and 2 s
2 CONC isters. Leonard is survived by 2 sons: Delbert of St. Maries, Idaho and Dale of Redwood City, California; 2 daughters: Arlyne - Mrs. Donald Gasaway of Mason City, Iowa and Colleen Bower of Stockton, California; 8 grandchildren; 2 
2 CONC great grandchildren; 1 brother: Oren Jackson of Manly, Iowa; other relatives and friends. Funeral services were held at the Warner Chapel in Spencer, Iowa, on Monday, October 4, 1982, at 10:00 a.m. with interment at Memorial Park 
2 CONC Cemetery in Mason City, Iowa at 2:00 p.m. Cause of death: acute respiratory failure.
