1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary:   Arlyne Virginia Gasaway MASON CITY -- Arlyne Virginia Gasaway, 76, of 907 N. Harrison Ave., died Saturday (Nov. 15, 1997) at Muse Norris Hospice Inpatient Unit. A funeral service will be held at 11 a.m. Tuesday at Hoga
2 CONC n Bremer Colonial Chapel, 126 Third St. N.E., with the Robert Cummings of Bethel United Methodist Church, Manly, and the Rev. Dennis Cahill of Hold Family Catholic Church, Mason City, officiating.  Burial will be in Memorial Park 
2 CONC Cemetery. Visitation will be held from 5 to 7 p.m. today at the funeral chapel, and will continue on Tuesday until service time. Arlyne Virginia Gasaway was born March 27, 1921, in Jasper, Minn., the daughter of Leonard and Ada (G
2 CONC illeland) Jackson.   She married Donald Gasaway on Feb. 24, 1941, in Manly. Arlyne grew up in Manly and graduated from Manly High School in 1938. She had many cats and enjoyed raising flowers.  She was a member of the Bethel Unite
2 CONC d Methodist Church in Manly. Survivors include her husband, Donald L. Gasaway, Mason City; one son, Donald Dennis Gasaway, Marion, Ill.; one sister, Colleen Dillon and her husband, Kenneth, of Folsom, California; two brothers, Del
2 CONC bert Jackson and his wife, Jeanette, St. Marys,Idaho, and Dale Jackson and his wife, Lucille, of Tucson, Ariz.; one brother-in-law, John Gasaway, Concord, California; one sister-in-law, Barb Gasaway, Mason City; and several nieces
2 CONC  and nephews. She was preceded in death by her parents, two sisters-in-law and two brothers-in-law. She and Don lived in Columbus, Ohio during the war, but moved to Mason City upon their return and made Mason City her home until h
2 CONC er death.
