1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Don Arnold was born in McCallsburg, IA at the Charles Christian Farm just 1 mile west of McCallsburg, on the kitchen table (as I have been told).  Don grew up in McCallsburg, until the family moved out to Washingto
2 CONC n State, close to Sam & Julia Arnold.  They later returned to McCallsburg where Don has lived except for a short time. Don & Betty lived in Radcliffe, IA and in Long Beach, CA while Don was in the service.  He has lived at 105 S. 
2 CONC 1st street in McCallsburg for some 43 years now.  Don quit school in 8th grade in order to go to work driving a truck for his dad Cleo, hauling rock from the gravel pit.  He later joined the Navy and served during the Korean confl
2 CONC ict.  While on a ship he had some steel drop on him and break his legs.  He was in a cast in the Naval hospital for some 9 months, getting it healed due to complications.  It has caused him problems over the years needless to say.
2 CONC   After his enlistment in the Navy was over, he came back to Iowa and worked at the Canning Factory in Roland for a while plus a couple other odd jobs before getting hired on at the Farmers Coop in McCallsburg.  He worked there fo
2 CONC r some 30+ years before having to retire due to his leg & knee problems.  Don lost his wife Betty on January 14, 2000.  He still misses her so today, and always will.  They were together for 47 years.    
