2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/100796690/guri-henryson
2 CONT
2 CONT Guri Gronstad Henryson BIRTH	28 Dec 1824 Etnesjoen, Etne kommune, Hordaland fylke, Norway DEATH	6 Apr 1909 (aged 84) Story City, Story County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Story City Cemetery Story City, Story County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT From Nevada Representative April 9, 1909
2 CONT
2 CONT County Correspondence
2 CONT
2 CONT STORY CITY
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Torkel Henryson died Thursday afternoon at her home after an illness of but a few days. The funeral service is held this Friday afternoon. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was born in Norway December 28, 1824 and was married to Torkel Henryson in April 11, 1847. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. and Mrs. Henryson came to this country and lived in Illinois until the spring of 1865 when they removed to Iowa. They located on their farm northeast of Story City where they made their home until 1892, when they moved to town
2 CONC . 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ten children were born to them, five dying in childhood. Two daughters, Mrs. Geo. Larson and Mrs. Sam Olson preceded their mother to the better land after they moved to Iowa. Beside the sorrowing husband three sons survive to mour
2 CONC n the loss of an affectionate mother, namely O. T. Henryson, who is a prosperous farmer north of town, T. T. and H. T. Henryson who are in the banking business. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her departure is a hard blow to her husband whose companion she has been for more than half a century. Had she lived until April 11 they would have been married 62 years. Mrs. Henryson was a God fearing woman all her life and to h
2 CONC er faith was no doubt attributable the placidity of mind and heart which led to long and useful life.
2 CONT
