2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/103797305/betsey-thorsbakken
2 CONT
2 CONT Daughter of Sakarias Sydness and Gurrie Vaugh.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Nevada Evening Journal Tuesday, May 29, 1951
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral Services For Mrs. Betsey Thorsbakken
2 CONT
2 CONT Funeral services for Mrs. Betsey Thorsbakken will be held Tuesday, May 29, at the Larson-Peterson Funeral home at 1:30 and at the Immanuel Lutheran church at 2 o'clock with Rev. A. O. Skibsrud presiding. Mrs. Thorsbakken, who had 
2 CONC been living with her daughter, Mr. Thomas Solbrack in Jewell, died Saturday at 12:20 p.m., at the age of 85, and due to a cerebral hemorrhage, three weeks ago. She had been living among her children for the last three years. Mrs. 
2 CONC Thorsbakken was born in Norway but had lived in the Story City community for many years. Her husband, Ole, died in 1940. She is survived by one daughter, Mrs. Solbrack of Jewell, four sons, Otis of Randall, Arthur of Alden and Hen
2 CONC ry and Selmer of Story City, two brothers in Norway and two sisters, Mrs. P. C. Peterson of Deer Creek, Minn. and Mrs. Lambert Stole of Minneapolis, Minn., 20 grandchildren and 18 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Nevada Evening Journal June 4, 1951 (page 4)
2 CONT
2 CONT Last Rites Wednesday For Mrs. Thorsbakken
2 CONT
2 CONT STORY CITY--Funeral services for Mrs. Betsey Thorsbakken were conducted Wednesday, May 30, at 1:30 in the Larson-Peterson Funeral home and 2:00 in the Immanuel church with the Rev. A. O. S---srud in charge. Special music of the ch
2 CONC urch service included a rendering of "The Lord's Prayer" by Emmet Olson of Jewell and "Den Store Hvide Flok" by Pastor S--bsrud.
2 CONT
2 CONT A large number of Memorial gifts in memory of Mrs. Thorsbakken were gratefully acknowledged and members of the bereaved family and friends were guests of Immanuel Ladies Aid for light refreshments served following the postal servi
2 CONC ce.
2 CONT
2 CONT Pall bearers were Herman Haugland, Arnold Erickson, Melbourne Henderson, Herman Wicks, Mayer Johnson and Gaylord Henryson. Burial was in the Fairview cemetery of Story City.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Betsey Thorsbakken was born in Sonderland, Norway, August 30, 1866 to the parents, Sokarias and Buri Sydness. At the age of 14 she emigrated to America and arrived in the vicinity of Story City, Ia., in 1881, to make her home
2 CONC  with an older sister.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1891 she was united in marriage to Ole Thorsbakken of Story City. Together with her husband, she made her home on a farm north and east of Story City. Accepting the privations of a pioneer wife, she faithfully helped her husban
2 CONC d in the business of making a home and clearing the acres of their farmland. To their union six children were born. One child, a daughter Clara died in infancy. The five children left to mourn her passing are her daughter, Mabel (
2 CONC Mrs. Thomas Solbrack of Jewell) and her sons Selmer and Henry of Story City, Otis of Randall and Arthur of Alden. Also surviving are two brothers Tollef and Christopher Sydness of Norway, two sisters, Mrs. Lambert Stole, Minneapol
2 CONC is, Minn. and Mrs. P. C. Peterson of Deer Creek, Minn. and 20 grandchildren and 18 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT After an illness of several months, Mrs. Thorsbakken passed away at the home of her daughter, Mrs. Thomas Solbrack at Jewell on May 26 at the age of 84 years, ten months and 26 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mrs. Thorsbakken was baptized and confirmed in the Christian faith in the Lutheran church in Norway. She was charter member of the Immanuel Congregation in Story City in which congregation she was a faithful member to the time of 
2 CONC her passing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Together with her many immediate relatives, Mrs. Thorsbakken endeared herself to a host of friends who also mourn her passing. May God Bless her memory.
