2 CONT According to the Twelfth Census of the United States, Schedule No. 1. - Population, for the state of Missouri, Livingston County, Grand River Township, on the 27 of June, 1900, Charles E. Jackson was listed as a farmer who operate
2 CONC d and owned a mortgaged farm, was married to Estella for 9 years, and had 4 living children.  He was born in December 1855 in Iowa, his father in Iowa, and his mother in Kentucky. Both he and his wife, Estella, could read, write, 
2 CONC and speak English. Estella had attended school 4 months. Estella was born in July, 1872, in Iowa, her father in Michigan, and her mother in New York.  Their children's names and birth dates were: Carry E., daughter, August 1891, a
2 CONC ge 8 William L., son, August 1893, age 6 Ona M., daughter, October 1896, age 3 Charles O., son, May 1899, age 1
2 CONT * According to this census, Leonard's name was shown as William L. Jackson.
2 CONT
2 CONT Obituary for Charles Edward Jackson Birth: 	Dec. 19, 1855 Iowa, USA Death: 	Aug. 23, 1936 Cerro Gordo County Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Mason City Globe Gazette (Mason City, Iowa) 1936 August 26 Rites held for C.E. Jackson Burial in Memorial Park Cemetery Beside Late Wife CLEAR LAKE--Funeral services for Charles Edward Jackson, 80, were held at the Williams Funera
2 CONC l home Wednesday at 2 p.m. with the Rev. H.O. Urness conducting the rites. Burial was in Memorial Park Cemetery besides the remains of Mrs. Jackson who died in June 1936. Mr. Jackson, who had been ailing for some time, died Sunday
2 CONC  morning at the home of his daughter, Mrs. J. M. Daniels, East Lake place, where he had been making his home for several months. He had previously lived in Springfield, Nebr., Wheeling, Mo., and Gowrie and Terrill, Iowa. Mr. Jacks
2 CONC on, who was born Dec. 19, 1855 and was married Miss Estella Hoyt in November, 1890, is survived by four children. Besides Mrs. Daniels they are Leonard Jackson, Manly, Ora Jackson, Sioux Rapids, and Mrs. Ona Davis, Austin, Minn. I
2 CONC n addition to his children he leaves a brother, David Lafayette (Lief) Jackson, St. Cloud, Minn., a sister. Mrs. Emma Switzer, Wheeling Mo., 23 grandchildren and 5 great grandchildren.
2 CONT
2 CONT Clifford Vik, accompanied by Miss Genevieve Hansen, sang appropriate selections and six grandsons were pallbearers.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family links: Spouse: Estella Marie Hoyt Jackson (1872 - 1936)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children: Carrie Elizabeth Jackson Daniel (1891 - 1978)*
