2 CONT "Obituary of Carrie Daniel," Estherville Daily News, Estherville, Emmet County, Iowa, Friday, June 16, 1978, Obituary section. 1891 - 1978 Estherville -- Carrie Elizabeth Daniel, 86, Estherville, passed away June 14 at Rosewood Ma
2 CONC nor Nursing Home, Estherville. Services for Mrs. Daniel were held at 2 p.m. Friday, June 16, at the Seventh Day Adventist Church, Spencer, Iowa. Burial was in Riverside cemetery, Spencer. Henry and Olson Funeral Home, Estherville,
2 CONC  was in charge of arrangements. She was born August 30, 1891, in Springfield, Nebraska to Charles and Estella Jackson. The family later moved to Iowa where Carrie was united in marriage May 11, 1911, with Joseph Marion Daniel. The
2 CONC  couple moved to the Langdon area in 1939 and to the Estherville area in 1942. They moved to Estherville in 1949. She was a member of the Seventh Day Adventist Church, Estherville, and is survived by four sons, Verl and Leonard, b
2 CONC oth of Spencer, Virgil, Des Moines, and Francis, Aberdeen, SD; three daughters, Mrs. Nellie Mustard, Estherville, Mrs. Rex (Ether) Moore, Spencer, and Mrs. Don (Leona) Daniel Daniel, Nevada; 40 grandchildren, 64 great-grandchildre
2 CONC n and seven great-great-granchildren; and two brothers Leonard Jackson, Carlisle, and Oren Jackson, Manly. Preceding her in death were her parents, her husband in 1959, one sister, one son and one daughter.
