1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Obituary in Mason City Globe Gazette, June 18, 1998:
2 CONT DONALD L. GASAWAY
2 CONT Mason City - Donald L. Gasaway, 80, of 907 N. Harrison Ave., died Tuesday (June 16, 1998) at the Muse Norris Hospice Inpatient Unit.
2 CONT A funeral Mass will be held at 10:30 Friday at Holy Family Catholic Church, 714 N. Adams Ave., with the Rev. Dennis Cahill, officiating. Burial will be in Memorial Park Cemetery, Mason City.
2 CONT Visitation will begin at 5 p.m. today at Hogan Bremer Colonial Chapel, 126 Third St., N.E., Mason City, with a Scriptural prayer service beginning at 6:30 p.m. followed by a Knights of Columbus Rosary at 7 p.m.
2 CONT Donald L. Gasaway was born June 19, 1917, in Mason City, son of John and Nellie (Conroy) Gasaway.  He married Arlyne Virginia Jackson on Feb. 24, 1941, in Manly.
2 CONT Donald graduated from St. Joseph High School and Hamilton Business College.  He worked as parts manager at S&R Chevrolet for 45 years and then also worked for Schukei and Sedars Motors until retiring.
2 CONT Don was an avid golfer.  He enjoyed playing cribbage and walking in the mall.
2 CONT He was a member of Holy Family Catholic Church where he ushered for many years, and also a member of the Knights of Columbus Council 1006, Mason City.
2 CONT Survivors include his son, Donald D. Gasaway, of Marion, IL; one brother, John Gasaway of Concord, CA; two sisters-in-law, Barb Gasaway, of Mason City, and Colleen Dillon and her husband, Kenneth, of Folsom, CA; and two brothers-i
2 CONC n-law, Delbert Jackson and his wife, Janet, of St. Marys, ID and Dale Jackson and his wife, Lucille, of Tucson, AZ; 13 nieces; seven nephews; and a long lifetime friend, Kenny Krieger, of Mason City.
2 CONT He was preceded in death by his parents; his wife, Arlyne on Nov. 15, 1997; two brothers, William and Charles Gasaway; one sister, Agnes Fitzgerald; and a sister-in-law, Laura Gasaway.
