1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT A kind and gentle man, Ken Dillon passed away suddenly, painlessly, on April 22, 2004. Born in Santa Monica on March 16, 1937, he was raised on a Virgil, Kansas farm and graduated from Virgil High School where he played on the bas
2 CONC ketball team. Immediately calling in the score after each game, he became a local "celebrity". His lief-long love and passion for basketball was evident in the fact that he was one of the first season-ticket holders of the Sacrame
2 CONC nto Kings. HIs favorite expression was "Go, Kings".
2 CONT
2 CONT Ken joined the army after high school, later returning to California to first graduate from American River College, then continued on to Sacramento State College in Psychology. He spent his life studying and enjoying people. Every
2 CONC where he went, he talked to everyone, and befriended many. Being civic-minded, Jen was a Paul Harris Award recipient of the Folsom Rotary Club, and a member of the Elks Club. He worked for Aerojet, then at McClennan Air Force Base
2 CONC  as a project manager for over 30 years, along with establishing a part-time DJ business. He enhanced many lives through his music, celbrating special events in their lives.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ken was a beloved family man, survived by his wife Colleen, daughter Cozette, son-in-law Gerry, granddaughters Danielle and Nicole, his mother Katherine, sister Linda, Brother-in-law John and their children Dan and Suzy and their 
2 CONC spouses, Rachel and Mike. They will miss him greatly.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ken said, "Life is precious". He was and will always be precious to us.
