1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Kvinnherad Gards- og ættesoga 2 page 408 (34c), page 394 (16).
2 CONT
2 CONT To America 1866.
2 CONT
2 CONT From "Find A Grave": Anna Torbjornsdotter Oyre
2 CONT
2 CONT BIRTH	4 May 1834 Kvinnherad kommune, Hordaland fylke, Norway DEATH	12 Jul 1866 (aged 32) Calamus, Clinton County, Iowa, USA BURIAL	 Kvindherred Cemetery Calamus, Clinton County, Iowa, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Torbjørnsdotter Øyre, daughter of Torbjørn Jensson Øyre (1802 - 1878) and Kristi Tørresdotter Vetlekre (1804 - 1893), was born on the Øyre farm in Kvinnherad’s Ænes parish, Hordaland, Norway. The parish register entered her b
2 CONC irth date as 4 May 1834 and her baptism as 8 May 1834. She was confirmed 12 Nov 1849 in the Kvinnherad church at Rosendal, Hordaland, Norway. She married Lars Johansen Flatebø from the neighboring Flatebø farm on 11 Oct 1854 in th
2 CONC e Ænes church, Ænes, Hordaland, Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT The parish register records the births of six children to Anna and Lars: 1. Sofie, 1855-, 2. Kristi, 1857-, 3. Johan Daniel, 1859-, 4. Karen, 1860-, 5. Guro, 1862-, 6. Jens, 1865-.
2 CONT
2 CONT The family emigrated to America in 1866. The parish register dates their departure from the parish April 1866. They departed Bergen 27 April 1866 on the bark Martha and arrived in Quebec on June 12. From there they traveled on to 
2 CONC the Norwegian settlement in Olive township, Clinton County, Iowa. Anna died shortly thereafter on 12 July 1866.
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Lars Johansen Flatebo 1834–1878 (m. 1854)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Carrie L. Johnson Andersen 1860–1937
2 CONT
2 CONT Julia Larsdatter Johnson Johnson 1862–1936
2 CONT
2 CONT Inscription ANNA T kone til Lars Johans död den 12 July 1866 32 Jaar gammel [Norwegian text at bottom undeciphered]
