1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Gards- og ættesoga for Haa I page 404 Njølstad (14.4).
2 CONT
2 CONT Nikolai bodde i Minnesota, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/64756082/nicolai-pedersen
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolai Pedersen BIRTH	28 Aug 1860 Hå kommune, Rogaland fylke, Norway DEATH	16 Sep 1940 (aged 80) Yellow Medicine County, Minnesota, USA BURIAL	 Spring Creek Lutheran Cemetery Yellow Medicine County, Minnesota, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Members
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse Gustava Lende Pedersen 1866–1953 (m. 1886)
2 CONT
2 CONT Children Christine Pederson Ree 1887–1917
2 CONT
2 CONT Grethe Marie Pedersen Paul 1889–1936
2 CONT
2 CONT Nora Josephine Pedersen Mossige 1891–1987
2 CONT
2 CONT Oscar O. Peterson 1893–1980
2 CONT
2 CONT Ella Maria Pedersen Berdeen 1895–1951
2 CONT
2 CONT Ruth Pedersen Jacobson 1897–1951
2 CONT
2 CONT Nettie Peterson Wait 1899–1996
2 CONT
2 CONT Martin Leonard Peterson 1903–1979
2 CONT
2 CONT Sylvia Margaret Pedersen Miller 1905–2003
2 CONT
2 CONT Born in Haa Norway Immigrated from Norway to USA in abt 1880 Naturalized U.S. Citizen
2 CONT
2 CONT *******************
2 CONT
2 CONT Spouse: Gustava Lende Pedersen 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Nicolai & Gustava: (known) Christine Pedersen Ree Grethe Marie Pedersen Paul Nora Josephine Pedersen Mossige Oscar O. Peterson Ella Maria Pedersen Berdeen Ruth Pedersen Jacobson Nettie Peterson Wait Martin Leonard Pete
2 CONC rson Sylvia Pedersen Miller George Peterson Bergliot Esther Pedersen Larson
2 CONT
2 CONT ( Some Children used Pedersen, others Peterson spelling.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Grandchildren: (many) Valette G. Ree McKibben Alice Leona Ree Kleve
2 CONT
2 CONT (Many Grandchildren and Great Grandchildren)
2 CONT
2 CONT *******************
2 CONT
2 CONT ** In Loving Memory of Nicolai ** Nicolai will be loved, missed and remembered in the hearts by all who loved him forever. Nicolai immigrated to the USA from Norway. He married Gustava Lende in Minnesota. Nicolai and Gustava lived
2 CONC  in  Yellow Medicine Co.MN. They raised their Children in Yellow Medicine Co. MN. Nicolai is survived by many relatives.
2 CONT
2 CONT -- - - - - - - - - - 
2 CONT
2 CONT Some documents spell Pedersen with  an "o" as Pederson. Nicolai's Grave Monument Marker is spelled Pedersen. Spellings for other family also Peterson, Petersen after Immigration to USA. variations.
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnesota Death Index: Nicolai Pedersen DOD: Sept. 16, 1940 Death County: Yellow Medicine MN Certificate: 017974
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. Evangelical Lutheran Church of America Records 1875-1940 site Nicolai's marriage to Gustava. Marriage Jan. 25, 1886 Cottenwood Hanley Falls MN Yellow Medicine Lutheran Church Married Gustava Lende Gustava's Parents Ole O. Len
2 CONC de and Gretta Lende Nicolai's Parents: Napoleon Pedersen Argel James Jensen (Pedersen) Original record sites Nicolai Pdersen place of birth Haa Norge (Norway)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Parents names not be transcribed accurate, especially Mother's name see Cemetery Records for Parents names original copy hard to read, also sited Haa Norge Olaus Leude. (sp))
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Minnesota Marriages Index: Nicolai's marriage to Gustava Lende Jan. 25, 1886 in Lucus, Lyon Co. MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT U.S. ELCA Lutheran Church Records site the Family was active at Silo Lutheran Church in Cottonwood MN and Spring Creek Lutheran Church in Clarksfield MN.(Normania Twp.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Spring Creek Lutheran Church Normania Township Yellow Medicine County Minnesota Church Cemetery Records site: Nicolai Pedersen Aug. 28, 1860- Sept. 16, 1940 Son of Napoleon and Axeliana (Jensen) Nostad Born in Haa Norway
2 CONT
2 CONT (Likely Haa Parish in Rogaland Norway Formerly Stavenger. Rogaland borders Hordaland and Telemark Norway)
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 U.S. Federal Census Friendship Yellow Medicine MN Sites Nicolai head of household Farmer in Farm Industry. He was the Employer. Nicolai was  was Married to Gustava. Nicoai Immigrated to USA in 1880. Nicolai and his Parents we
2 CONC re born in Norway. Gustava and her Parents were born in Norway. Gustava immigrated from Norway to the USA in 1879. Both Nicolai and Gustava were naturalized U.S. Citizens. Census Report included their children. .  Nicolai's Mother
2 CONC s name is spelled differently on different records.
2 CONT ---
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900 U.S. Federal Census Friendship, Yellow Medicine MN Nicolai Pedersen married, head of household living with Spouse Gustava and their many children. (Original spelled Pederson, transcribed as Cederson.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1905 Minnesota Census sites Nicolai Pedersen living in Friendship MN.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 U.S. Federal Census  Friendship Yellow Medicine MN Nicolai Pedersen married, head of household Farmer sites Nicolai's large Family. They lived in Friendship Yellow Medicine MN. All the children born in Minnesota.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1920 U.S. Federal Census Friendship Yellow, Medicine MN Nicolai Pederson married, head of household Farmer Nicolai age 59, Gustava 54,and children Ella M. Pederson 24, M. Leonard Pederson 16, Sylvia M. Pederson 14, E. Bergliot Ped
2 CONC erson 12 yrs old. Granddaughter Alice L. Ree age 6 yrs. ( spelled with o on Census) 
2 CONT
2 CONT 1930 U.S. Federal Census Granite Falls, Chipewa Co. MN Nicolai Pederson married, head of household Farmer living with Spouse Gustava Pedersen
2 CONT
2 CONT 1940 U.S. Federal Census Friendship, Yellow Medicine MN Nicolai married, head of household living with Spouse Gustava and Son Leonard Pedersen Nicolai Pedersen 79 yrs Gustava Pedersen 74 yrs Leonard Pedersen 36 yrs
2 CONT
2 CONT (to note, most Census reports transcribed as Pederson vs. Pedersen spelling)
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Nicolai and Gustava's Daughter  Christine Pedersen Ree  Spouse: Arnt Ree Christine passed away in 1917  from Tuberculosis. (T.B.)
2 CONT
2 CONT Christine and Arnt Ree Children: Alice Ree and Valette Ree .  It appears Christine's daughter Alice  was staying with Nicolai and Gustava in 1920.  Christine's daughter Valetta Ree was living with her Father and Step Mother Lettie
2 CONC  Ree in Kildeer, Dunn North Dakota in 1920. (and Hugo Ree, Lettie Martin Ree's Father Charles Martin who was born in Denmark) By 1930 Census, Arnt Ree, a Widower remarried (1919). Arnt Ree, Spouse Lettie, children Valette, Alice a
2 CONC nd  Hugo Ree lived in Eugene, Lane Co. Oregon.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1910 Christina was married to Arnt Ree in Dunn North Dakota. They had one child Valetta Ree age 1 yrs old in 1910. Not known where Christine passed away. Possibly North Dakota. Christine and Arnt Ree had two Children;  Alice an
2 CONC d Valette Ree, both born in in North Dakota. Arnt Ree remarried as a Widower to Lettie in 1919. Lettie's Son Hugo grew up with Valette and Alice Ree. Hugo , born in 1910, went by  Hugo Ree and was part of the Ree Family. Their Ree
2 CONC  Family moved to Oregon.  Alice Ree Kleve was living in Susanville California in 1977 per Arnt's obituary. Lettie Ree preceded Arnt Ree in death. Christines name was left out of Arnt's Obituary but included in Valette's Obituary. 
2 CONC (See Valette's Memorial. Valette Ree McKibben's Obituary includes some Family information). Christine was born in Minnesota in 1887. Christine married Arnt Ree in Maynard Minnesota in 1908. Daughter Valette Ree was a Teacher and D
2 CONC aughter Alice Ree was a Nurse. Alice Ree born abt 1914 was a Nurse in California by 1940 Census. Alice was also a U.S. Military Veteran.
2 CONT
2 CONT Christine Pedersen Ree's 1917 Funeral services were held at the Spring Creek Lutheran Church in Clarksfield MN per the ELCA Lutheran Church archive records. Christine is laid to rest with her Parents.
2 CONT
2 CONT Alice Leona Ree Kleve 1913 N.D.- 1996 Nevada Memorial: 108676202 Second Lt. U.S. Army Military grave marker Spouse Emil WWII Military  grave marker also.
2 CONT
2 CONT (Matches Arnt Ree's Obituary data, Census data, SSA and Death Index info. Born in North Dakota, passed away in Reno Nevada, last resided in Susanville California Public City Directories, Census reports as child Alice L. Ree. Spous
2 CONC e Emil Kleve who has a Memorial. Jeffery Kleve also laid to rest at the same Calif. Cemetery. Emil last resided in Susanville California, as did Alice. Nevada Death Index same data as birth record dob's SSA dates, Public data came
2 CONC  dob's and Susanville California. Alice and Emil's Son Jeffrey Wayne Kleve's  California Birth records and  Death records both site Mothers Maiden name: Ree. ) Edits and Links requested.
2 CONT
2 CONT --
2 CONT
2 CONT Written Memorials Tributes, photos, Family  history welcome for Nicolai's Memorial.
